From 1afc8ec5714753b39892dd842133b9b8978e9ef7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 19:22:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/22] riscv: mm: fix the XIP trampoline mapping on 32-bit

On !64BIT (Sv32, folded PMD) the trampoline page directory is always
populated with kernel_map.phys_addr, i.e. the RAM copy of the data
section. For XIP kernels the text executes in place from flash at
kernel_map.xiprom; mapping the kernel virtual base to RAM means the
very first instruction fetched after satp is switched to the
trampoline decodes from data bytes, and boot dies in an endless
illegal-instruction loop.

Mirror the 64-bit code, which already special-cases XIP, and map the
trampoline to kernel_map.xiprom on XIP.

32-bit XIP has never booted past this point.

Co-developed-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/riscv/mm/init.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/mm/init.c b/arch/riscv/mm/init.c
index 15b2eda4c..5c9e18467 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/mm/init.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/mm/init.c
@@ -1214,8 +1214,13 @@ asmlinkage void __init setup_vm(uintptr_t dtb_pa)
 #endif
 #else
 	/* Setup trampoline PGD */
+#ifdef CONFIG_XIP_KERNEL
+	create_pgd_mapping(trampoline_pg_dir, kernel_map.virt_addr,
+			   kernel_map.xiprom, PGDIR_SIZE, PAGE_KERNEL_EXEC);
+#else
 	create_pgd_mapping(trampoline_pg_dir, kernel_map.virt_addr,
 			   kernel_map.phys_addr, PGDIR_SIZE, PAGE_KERNEL_EXEC);
+#endif
 #endif
 
 	/*
